@startuml tool4-early-warning
title Tool 4 - Early warning (schema-drift guard)

skinparam shadowing false
left to right direction

queue "DATA STREAM\n(Kafka topic)\n--\nfield 'price'\njust became text\ninstead of number" as K #FFF3E0
rectangle "EARLY WARNING\n--\nwatches quietly,\nlearns the normal\nshape of the data" as W #FFE0B2
rectangle "YOU\n--\n'Heads up: topic X changed.\nIt will break file\norders.py line 42.'" as U #FFF3E0

K -right-> W : reads a tiny sample
W -right-> U : alert in under a minute

note bottom of W
  It does not just say 'something changed'.
  It names the exact service and line of code
  that will break - before it actually breaks.
end note
@enduml
